#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:5
#: 93a8dad3f1314ceaa9502287d011eee8
msgid "Circle Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:7
#: 95df855bb80e49bdb8d29240dafd8089
msgid "Circle will orbit a point located :ref:`CIRC_RADIUS<CIRC_RADIUS>` meters in front of the vehicle when the mode is entered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:10
#: 15458835b0dc4bff9a95e094a0016372
msgid "Setting the :ref:`CIRC_RADIUS<CIRC_RADIUS>` to zero will cause the rover to simply stay in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:13
#: c2474a6e4bfe47069a5d988767680cb6
msgid "The speed of the vehicle (in meters/second) is set by the :ref:`CIRC_SPEED<CIRC_SPEED>` parameter. And the direction is set by the :ref:`CIRC_DIR<CIRC_DIR>` parameter, \"0\" is CW, \"1\" CCW."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:17
#: 16ffab5fe5a5469299506937345f93a1
msgid "Operation Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:19
#: 87399d245546491c8d6b51f290871436
msgid "The target point moving around the circle does not slowdown if the vehicle cannot keep up. This means that a too high a :ref:`CIRC_RADIUS<CIRC_RADIUS>` parameter value will lead to the vehicle driving at full throttle inside the desired radius."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/circle-mode.rst:20
#: 712380de0e28486cb341245353f542ac
msgid "The radius, speed and direction parameters only take effect when the vehicle enters circle mode (or begins a LOITER_TURNS mission command) so users cannot easily change the radius or direction while in the mode. Instead they must exit and re-enter the mode. In missions, the speed can be changed using the DO_CHANGE_SPEED MAVlink or mission command."
msgstr ""
